# QA Automation Demo

A small end-to-end QA automation project covering API testing, UI testing, and CI/CD — built to get hands-on practice with tools beyond what I used in my capstone (pytest, SQL) and co-op (unit testing, automated validation).

## What This Project Tests

**API tests** (`test_api.py`) — automated tests against the [dummyjson.com](https://dummyjson.com) REST API, covering:
- Listing resources and validating response schema
- Fetching a single resource by ID
- Field-selection query parameters (`?select=`)
- Search functionality (`?q=`), asserting results are actually relevant to the query, not just that the request succeeded
- Full CRUD: create (POST), update (PUT), delete (DELETE)
- A negative test case — verifying correct behavior when requesting a nonexistent resource

**UI tests** (`test_ui.py`) — Playwright browser automation against the official [Playwright TodoMVC demo app](https://demo.playwright.dev/todomvc), covering:
- Adding an item
- Completing an item
- Deleting an item

Locators use Playwright's recommended user-facing strategies (`get_by_role`, `get_by_placeholder`, `get_by_text`) rather than brittle CSS/XPath selectors, for better resilience to markup changes.

**Manual exploration** — a Postman collection (see `postman/` if exported) covering the same API endpoints with response assertions, used to explore and validate behavior before automating it in pytest.

## Tools Used

- **pytest** — test runner and assertions
- **requests** — HTTP client for API tests
- **Playwright (Python)** — browser automation for UI tests
- **Postman** — manual/exploratory API testing
- **GitHub Actions** — CI pipeline

## Running Locally

```bash
python3 -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install pytest requests pytest-playwright
playwright install

pytest test_api.py -v
pytest test_ui.py -v
```

## Continuous Integration

This project runs its full test suite automatically on every push and pull request via GitHub Actions (`.github/workflows/tests.yml`). The workflow checks out the code, installs dependencies (including Playwright's browser binaries), and runs both the API and UI test suites, reporting pass/fail status on each commit.

Note: the workflow currently runs tests and reports status; it is not yet wired into a branch protection rule, so it doesn't block merges on failure — that would be the natural next step to turn this into an enforced quality gate rather than just a signal.

## Why This Project

Built as focused, hands-on practice to complement my testing experience from my capstone project (a clinic management system with 239 pytest tests, Jest, Locust load testing, and security/RBAC testing) and my co-op at Eli Lilly (automated data validation and unit testing in ASP.NET Core). This project applies the same risk-based, edge-case-first testing mindset to a new toolset — Postman, Playwright, and CI — in a small, complete, and demonstrable way.